{
  "name": "Domes",
  "_about": "A DOME IS AN ARCH TURNED ABOUT ITS AXIS: its meridian is the right half of an arch profile over its own span, so every head the engine has is also a dome -- the hemisphere (semicircular), the lowered or saucer dome (segmental), the Gothic (pointed), the Moorish that swells past its springing (horseshoe), the onion and the bell (the S-line of two radii, with and without a bulge), the cone (trigonal) and the flared spire (inflexed). Left without `sides` a dome is ROUND and its facets follow the detail level (+ and -); given `sides` it is a cloister vault of that many webs, as Florence's eight. `thickness` 0 is a skin, the way a roof is built; otherwise two shells of masonry. None of these has ribs: ribs are laid ON a dome by a part of their own (see the ribbed dome).",
